ker). Similarly, attaching ♦A or ♦K is unnecessary here — the landlord likely holds higher cards if they\'re trying to push sequences now.\n\nInstead, I should use the minimal sufficient card to win while preserving flexibility. Since the landlord played triple 6s + 5, any triple 8s + single beats it — even with a low kicker. So using a low card like ♥3, ♥4, or ♥5 is acceptable.\n\nBetween them, ♥3 is the lowest and safest discard. It doesn’t signal strength and preserves slightly better balance.\n\nThus, the best move is: **triple_with_single: ♥3 ♠8 ♥8 ♦8**\n\nReason: I must beat the landlord’s triplet with single attachment. I choose to do so efficiently by using the weakest possible attached card (♥3) with my triple 8s, minimizing waste of high-value cards for future plays. This maintains hand strength for later opportunities to help my teammate or block the landlord.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥3", "♠8", "♥8", "♦8"]}'}
